hadiths[48]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3862","Amr bin Shu'ayb narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Zahar does not occur with female slaves."
"3863","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Zahar does not occur with a maidservant."
"3864","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) was asked about a person who makes Zahar with his four wives, and he said, his expiation will be only one."
"3865","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this saying of Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA): When a person has four wives and he performs zahar with all of them, he will have to pay only one Kaffarah."
"3866","Aisha bint Talha narrates: I said: If I marry Mus'ab bin Zubair, he will be my father's back (respectable as) to me. Then he inquired about his command, so he was instructed to free a slave, then he married Mus'ab bin Zubair."
"3867","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar (may Allah be pleased with him) married a daughter of Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and a wife of Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who belonged to the Nahshal tribe (i.e. he married a girl and her stepmother)."
"3868","A narrator named Muhammad narrates: A Companion from Egypt named Habla married a man's wife and had a daughter by that man's second wife. A narrator named Ayyub narrates: Sayyiduna Hasan Basri has called it makruh."
"3869","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, says: Khula, separation, has to happen, it is not divorce."
"3870","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used medicine to bring together a husband and wife who had previously been divorced and divorced."
"3871","Ata narrates: A woman came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she complained about her husband. Al-Walid has quoted a different chain of transmission regarding Ibn Jarih, he has quoted it from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Ata, but its sender is correct."
"3872","Jamhan narrates: During the caliphate of Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA), Sayyida Umm Bakra Aslamah (RA) obtained Khula from her husband, then Sayyidna 'Uthman (RA) said: This will count as a divorce, but if the two of them have decided on something else, then it will be (counted) according to what they have decided."
"3873","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A woman who gets Khula can get Khula in exchange for something worth less than her father."
"3874","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: A woman's pregnancy cannot remain in her womb for more than two years, even if she changes as much as the shadow of a spinning wheel."
"3875","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: A woman's pregnancy cannot remain in her womb for more than two years, even if she is changed as much as spinning wood. A woman named Jamila Bint Saad is the sister of Ubaid Bin Saad."
"3876","A narrator named Abu Sufyan narrates: Some of our elders narrated this: A man came to the service of Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab and said: O Amir al-Mu’minin, after two years he came to his wife and she was pregnant. Sayyidna Umar R.A. consulted the people about stoning this woman, then Sayyidna Mu’adh bin Jabal R.A. said: O Amir al-Mu’minin, you can punish this woman, but you cannot punish the child in her womb. So you leave her until she gives birth to a child. Sayyiduna Umar left her. She gave birth to a boy whose front teeth protruded outwards, as a result of which the person found out that the child resembled him. He said: By the Lord of the Kaaba! This is my son, then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: Women have become unable to give birth to a child like Mu'az. If Mu'az had not been there, Umar would have been killed."
"3877","Waleed bin Muslim narrates: I said to Imam Malik: I was told on the authority of Sayyida Aisha that she says that a woman can be pregnant for a maximum of two years, as long as the shadow of a wheel. So Imam Malik said: Subhan Allah, how can a person say this? This is our girl who is the wife of Muhammad bin Ajlan. She is a virtuous woman. Her husband is also a virtuous man. She has given birth to three children in twelve years."
"3878","Mubarak bin Mujahid narrates: It is known among us that the wife of Muhammad bin Ajlan used to give birth to children after being pregnant for four years."
"3879","Hashim bin Yahya narrates: Once Malik bin Dinar was sitting, a man came to him and said: O Abu Yahya: Pray for this woman who has been pregnant for four years and is in severe pain. If I am a girl, then change her into a boy, for You can destroy whom You will and retain whom You will, Umm Al-Katab, with You. Then Malik bin Dinar raised his hands, and the people also raised their hands. At the same time, a messenger came to the man and said, 'Go to your wife.'"
"3880","Uza'i says: We have a woman who menstruates in the morning and becomes pure in the evening."
"3881","Ubada bin Ibad Mehlabi narrates: There is a woman in our Mahlib tribe who became a grandmother at the age of eighteen, she gave birth to a girl at the age of Nabars, her daughter also gave birth to a daughter at the age of nine, that woman became a grandmother at the age of eighteen."
"3882","Bahria bint Hani bin Qubaysa narrates: I got married to Qaqaa bin Sur, he stayed with me for one night, then my father, who was a villager, submitted a case to the service of Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Messengers of Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him, came and took him with him to Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him, inquired whether you had intercourse with this woman. maintained."
"3883","Bahria bint Hani bin Qubaysa narrates that her father married her to a man who was a Christian. The woman herself married Qaqaa bin Sur. The girl's father came to Sayyidna Ali (RA). subjected me to disgrace, I did not want it, so Qaqa'a said: Do you think that I have secretly married? These people presented their case in front of Sayyidna Ali (RA), then Sayyidna Ali (RA) inquired, have you had intercourse with this woman? He replied yes, then Sayyiduna Ali (Radi Allahu Anhu) declared it right for this woman to marry herself. The woman named Bahria is unknown."
"3884","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a woman's guardian is harmful and she appoints another person as her guardian and he marries that woman, then his marriage will be valid."
"3885","Shaibani narrates: There was a woman in our neighborhood (in the neighborhood or tribe) whose name was Bahria. Her mother married her. Her father was not there at that time. When her father came, he denied the relationship. He presented this matter to Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and Sayyidna Ali (RA) maintained the marriage."
"3886","Abu Qais narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) gave this decision about this."
"3887","Hazeel narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) gave a decision accordingly."
"3888","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person said: O Messenger of Allah! Didn't Allah Ta'ala say: Divorce is done twice, then why is it ordered for the third time? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (Allah has also said this). ’’ Then one has to be restrained in a known manner or released with grace."
"3889","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I have heard Allah say: There will be two divorces, then where did the order for the third divorce come from? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (Allah has also said this). ” Then one has to stop in a known way, or release with favor (this refers to the third divorce). The narrator has quoted it on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, but it is true that this hadith has been transmitted on the authority of Ismail bin Sami, on the authority of Aburzeen, as a messenger tradition on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3890","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There are four ways of giving divorce, two of them are halal and two are haram. One halal method is: A man divorces a woman when she is in a state of purity (and the person has not had sexual intercourse with her during the period of purity). (One) Haraam method is that a man divorces a woman when she is menstruating (the second Haraam method is) A man divorces a woman in a state of purity when he has had intercourse with her, and he does not know whether there is a child in the womb or not."
"3891","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah way of giving divorce is that a man should give a divorce to a woman during every tahr, when it is completed, this is the ``Idah'' that Allah has ordered."
"3892","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A person who wants to divorce according to the Sunnah should divorce a woman when she is in a state of purity, and he has not had intercourse with her (he should also make someone witness when he divorces)."
"3893","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: I divorced my wife, she was in the state of menstruation at that time. Sayyidna Umar (RA) attended the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and asked him (about this issue). will The Prophet (PBUH) said yes."
"3894","Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: Sayyiduna Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) (after that he mentioned the previous hadith)."
"3895","Salem narrates about his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): He divorced his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was in the state of menstruation at that time. She does not become pure after another menstrual period, then if the group wishes to divorce her without cohabiting with her in a state of purity, this will be a divorce according to the method that Allah has ordered."
"3896","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: I divorced my wife who was menstruating. Sayyidna Umar mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace be upon him) expressed his displeasure, and said that he should return to this woman, then keep her with him until her next menstruation, which is other than the period in which he divorced her, then if he feels fit, then he should marry her. Divorce at the time when she is free from this next menses and before cohabiting with her, this divorce will be according to the method that Allah has ordered. Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) had given a divorce to this woman, this divorce was considered to be a divorce, then Hazrat Abdullah (RA) had approached this woman, as the Prophet (PBUH) had ordered him to do."
"3897","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) mentioned this to the Prophet (PBUH), and the Prophet (PBUH) expressed his displeasure about it. A narrator named Saleh has narrated these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed his displeasure about Sayyiduna Abdullah (after this the narrator mentioned the previous hadith)."
"3898","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah way of giving divorce is that a man divorces a woman when she is in a state of purity, and (in the midst of this purity) he has not had intercourse with her, or divorces her again when the woman's pregnancy becomes apparent."
"3899","It has been narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, Sayyidna Umar mentioned this issue to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said, Tell him to approach this woman and then divorce her when she is in a state of purity or pregnancy."
"3900","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Umar (RA): The Prophet (SAW) was told that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife during her menstruation."
"3901","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3902","Abu Zubair narrates: I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar about a person who divorces his wife during her menstruation, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar said: Do you know Ibn Umar? I replied yes. He said, I had given three divorces to my wife during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). All the narrators of this tradition are Shia. The safe tradition is this: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife during her menstruation."
"3903","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife during her menses. Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the Prophet (SAW) and told him about it. The Prophet (SAW) said to him, \Tell Abdullah to approach this woman"," and when she has performed ghusl"," (i.e. purified)"," he should let her stay like this until (the next time).\"" If he menstruates"," then when he takes a bath (i.e. cleans himself) from the next menstruation"," he should divorce her before having intercourse with her. If he wants to keep her with him"," then he should keep her with him. Ubaidullah narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to this woman during her menstruation"," but he did it contrary to the Sunnah method."""
"3904","Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: He divorced his wife and she was in the state of menstruation at that time. Menstruation comes and after that she becomes pure, then if he wants, he should divorce her before having intercourse with her, and if he wants, he should let her stay with him. Saleh bin Kaisan, Musa bin Uqbah, Ismail bin Umayyah, Laith bin Saad, Ibn Abi Zayb, Ibn Jarij, Jabir, Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated this from Sayyidina Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Nafi. Al-Zuhri has narrated the same thing about Salem from his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar). Yunus bin Jubir, Sha'bi and Hasan al-Basri have also narrated the same thing."
"3905","Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: A man came to the service of Sayyiduna Umar and said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating. A narrator named Ibn Sa'id narrates: A man said to Sayyiduna Umar (RA): I divorced my wife when she was menstruating. After that, the two narrators have narrated these words: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said, \You have disobeyed your Lord and your wife has separated from you.\"" That person said: When Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA) separated from his wife"," the Prophet (PBUH) did not instruct him to return to his wife. A narrator named Ibn Sa'id narrated these words: When Abdullah bin Umar (RA) separated from his wife during her period (i.e. divorced her)"," the Prophet (PBUH) told him to return to her. After that"," the two narrators have narrated these words: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to this person: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him (i.e. Ibn Umar RA) to return to his wife because of the divorce that remained (i.e."," which Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) still had the power to grant). A narrator named Ibn Sa`id narrated these words: He had appealed on the basis of the divorce"," which he still had the right to"," and you did not allow the matter to remain"," on the basis of which you could appeal to your wife. A narrator named Ibn Muni has quoted these words: There is nothing left for you on the basis of which you can approach your wife. Shaykh Abul Qasim has narrated this to us: This tradition has been narrated by many narrators: but they did not mention these words of Sayyiduna Umar in it"," as far as I know"," no other narrator has narrated this saying except Saeed bin Abdul Rahman."""
"3906","Abu Ghulab narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, did you count this divorce? Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar said, \Why didn't I count him? Was I humble?\"" Or was he stupid?"""
"3907","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: Twenty years ago, an authentic narrator narrated this hadith to me: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar divorced his wife three times during her menstruation, so he was ordered to return to her. I considered this tradition to be authentic, he told me this: He asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar about this, then Sayyidna Abdullah told him that he had divorced his wife during her menstruation, so he was ordered to return to that woman. So Syedna Abdullah said why not, was he humble?"
"3908","Yunus bin Jubayr narrates: He asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) how many divorces had he given to his wife? Sayyiduna Ibn Umar said:"
"3909","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar Z divorced his wife while she was menstruating. Sayyidna Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this issue, so the Prophet instructed him to approach the woman and keep her until she becomes pure again, then wait until she becomes pure again before having intercourse with her (divorce her). According to this order, women should be divorced."
